=======================================================================
 THE RULES A NEW TYPE MUST PASS
=======================================================================

1. It descends from one of the four roots. A type that extends
   nothing has no place to live and is a defect.

2. It goes in the directory of the root it descends from, in a file
   named after it, in a module named after that file's path.

3. A finite set of choices rides as an argument, never as a family of
   types. Over-relaxation is a number on gauss-seidel, not a class.
   An open set - materials, for instance - is a family and inherits.

4. A composite that existing types already express earns no name.

5. No abstract type without a concrete one that means something.

6. Two independent choices must give the same answer in either order,
   or they are not independent.


=======================================================================
 WHAT DOES NOT BELONG IN A BANNER
=======================================================================

A file's banner states only what the compiler can check: what the
type is, what it extends, what its procedures do. Anything the
compiler cannot check will drift into a lie. Design facts - which
stage of the pipeline a type serves, which level it was ruled to sit
at - live here, in one place, where one edit keeps them true.
